{{ end }}{{ if $queue }}## Messages

- Validate every message at the boundary: its body and the attributes the
  code reads, narrowed from `unknown` with runtime checks. The queue holds
  whatever a producer sent. [review]
- A message that fails throws, inside the work Powertools' batch processing
  runs per message: the batch reports it in `batchItemFailures`, SQS
  delivers it alone again, and after the queue's last delivery it waits in
  the dead-letter queue. [test: every SQS source reports batch item
  failures]
- Never catch a failure and carry on: a message the handler returns as
  done is deleted, and lost. [review]
- A message is delivered at least once and in no set order: the work per
  message is idempotent (Powertools' Idempotency, keyed by its `messageId`)
  and never depends on another message coming first. [review]
- Never log a message's body: it may hold user data. Log its `messageId`
  and what failed. [review]
