- Model the table for its access patterns: every read on a {{ if $queue }}message's{{ else }}request{{ end }} path is
  a `GetItem` or a `Query` on a key or an index, never a `Scan`. [review]
{{ if $go -}}
- Read and write items as `map[string]types.AttributeValue`, by hand or
  with `feature/dynamodb/attributevalue`; validate what a read returns
  before using it, since another writer may have stored something else.
  [review]
{{- else if $py -}}
- Use boto3's `Table` resource so items are plain dicts; numbers come back
  as `Decimal`. Validate what a read returns before using it, since another
  writer may have stored something else. [review]
{{- else -}}
- Use the document client (`@aws-sdk/lib-dynamodb`) so items are plain
  objects; validate what a read returns before using it, since another
  writer may have stored something else. [review]
